// An original example in a minor key and 6/8 time.
// In a minor key, 1 is the tonic: 1m is Em, b3 is G, b7 is D.

## Intro
> MD keys: Solo piano, rubato on the last bar.
1m | b6 | b3 | b7~

## Verse
> MD: Keep it soft. Feel two big beats per bar.
{p} 1m "Lanterns on the water" | b6 | b3 | b7
1m | b6 | 4m | 5

## Chorus
> MD: Lift here. Everyone in.
{mf} b3 | b7 | 1m | b6
b3 | b7 | 4m:3 5:3 | 1m

## Tag
> MD: Pull it down and hold the last chord on my cue.
{p} b6 | b7 | <1m>~
